#entry("builder:WP-08 (agent B)", "handoff", status: "done")[*Homes for the Lloyds brief (UI, brief-mandatory scope).* `/app/portfolio`: homes ranked by improvement potential (purchased energy, grid electricity plus gas), Poor and Very poor flagged with key issues, electricity and gas shown separately, "unavailable" without readings. `/app/portfolio/:id`: Green Home Score with band and a "why this score" table (weight, sub-score, contribution per component), prioritised feasible retrofits (High, Medium or Low, reason, per-fuel saving net of the ones above, increases negative), package after interactions, improvement potential, carbon by fuel (DESNZ 2024 factors shown), indicative value range, and a what-if (tick or untick a retrofit) that reruns every figure; the narrator only reads computed values. Nav link "Homes". *Stub:* `apps/web/src/portfolio/model.ts` is a local documented model and synthetic portfolio (P10001 to P10040, P10001 scores 38, Poor) until Agent A posts its interface; the swap is the two functions `portfolio()` and `analyseHome()` plus types. *Agent A:* please post the export names and shapes (score components, issues, retrofit list with suitability and per-fuel savings, package, carbon, value range, what-if entry point). *Tests:* web 5 files 35 passed (6 new: weights, P10001 band, monotone sub-scores, package equals listed savings, heat pump raises electricity, carbon identity, what-if rerun, unavailable handling, screens); typecheck clean; tools/lint clean.]
#entry("agent-C:WP-07", "handoff", status: "done")[*Studio round 4, scene (short pass, coordinator deadline).* R4-B2 fixed: the radiation rose (the unlabelled pinwheel on the hero roof) is removed from `CityScene.tsx`; the roof and wall colouring carries the Radiation lens. The three.js Clock deprecation warning on each canvas mount came from React Three Fiber 9 creating a `THREE.Clock` in its store, not from our code; `packages/scene/src/three/quiet.ts` filters that one message through three's `setConsoleFunction` and passes all others on (installed by `Stage` and `CityStage`). Not done this pass: R4-B5 thumbnail framing, R4-M1 Make split orientation and floor, chajja edge strength, night radiation paint, AO smudges, Building camera pitch. Note for B: compact thumbnails use `style="svg"` (a plan), which can never show chajjas or glazing; a 3D style with `level="building"` and `azimuthDeg` set to the changed facade's outward bearing (180 for a south facade) would show them. For Make split, `level="floor"` with `storeyId` already lifts the floors above, and `azimuthDeg={180}` looks north (north up). Tests: scene 107 passed (1 worker), tsc and Biome clean. No screenshots this pass.]
